(5583540, 807041, 94235, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the great comments.<br/>Tried and outside the box entry which was well accepted and appreciated by many.<br/>Unfortunately the stalwarts who believe that geology only consists of out-crops of rocks (don''t get me wrong there are some fantastic shots here) voted the other way.<br/>Starting to think originality is a punt you take on this site while the norm is the way to go to get an accepted, higher voted shot.<br/>Better go find myself a sunset or flower or bug or water drop or..............  ;-)<br/></td>', 'Thanks for all the great comments.Tried and outside the box entry which was well accepted and appreciated by many.Unfortunately the stalwarts who believe that geology only consists of out-crops of rocks (don''t get me wrong there are some fantastic shots here) voted the other way.Starting to think originality is a punt you take on this site while the norm is the way to go to get an accepted, higher voted shot.Better go find myself a sunset or flower or bug or water drop or..............  ;-)', '2009-07-22 19:51:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5583573, 807304, 98171, '<td valign="top">i chuckled at the "i hope this is not DNMC". See, when I first saw the photo, i thought "this is so not EROSION". I think I gave it maybe a 4. Then I stared at it, and it dawned on me that it was erosion, and that the picture is really amazing. I hated it at first because im sooo sick of the water-motion blur-beach photos. But this one is different. And I gave it a 10.<br/>After that novel....CONGRATS!</td>', 'i chuckled at the "i hope this is not DNMC". See, when I first saw the photo, i thought "this is so not EROSION". I think I gave it maybe a 4. Then I stared at it, and it dawned on me that it was erosion, and that the picture is really amazing. I hated it at first because im sooo sick of the water-motion blur-beach photos. But this one is different. And I gave it a 10.After that novel....CONGRATS!', '2009-07-22 20:29:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5583588, 806761, 60495, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kaiser_chief:</b></div><hr/><i> A nicely composed image.......The rocks though seem to have lost the detail though that really could have been a feature of this photo </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree the full size photo has plenty of detail in the rocks but to get it under the size limit I had to take it down below 55% so a lot of detail was lost.</td>', 'Originally posted by kaiser_chief: A nicely composed image.......The rocks though seem to have lost the detail though that really could have been a feature of this photo   I agree the full size photo has plenty of detail in the rocks but to get it under the size limit I had to take it down below 55% so a lot of detail was lost.', '2009-07-22 20:50:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5583596, 807191, 79955, '<td valign="top">Darn !!! don''t worry too much about this (easier said than done..). I have gone through this myself so I know how it feels. Take it as a learning process. As I have mentioned to many others including myself , a great shot is a great shot !!!!! That is the achievement and you know from the score that many has acknowledged that fact.<br/></td>', 'Darn !!! don''t worry too much about this (easier said than done..). I have gone through this myself so I know how it feels. Take it as a learning process. As I have mentioned to many others including myself , a great shot is a great shot !!!!! That is the achievement and you know from the score that many has acknowledged that fact.', '2009-07-22 20:59:43.000000', NULL, 0),
